# Follow the UWB-tracked person (served by uwb_follower on /uwb_follower/follow_person).
# Following runs until the goal is cancelled, or ends by itself when one of the limits
# below is reached. The robot stops when the goal ends. A new goal replaces the current
# one, and /uwb_follower/enable false aborts it.

# Goal
float32 follow_distance   # m behind the person along their path; 0 = the node's follow_distance
float32 max_duration_s    # succeed after this long; 0 = no limit
float32 lost_timeout_s    # abort if the person is lost for this long; 0 = keep waiting
---
# Result
float32 duration_s        # how long the goal ran
float32 distance_driven_m # how far the robot drove
string message            # why it ended
---
# Feedback
string state              # following, turning, waiting, obstacle, backing, blocked,
                          # unsticking, stuck, lost, no_estimate
float32 distance_to_person  # m along the trail (NaN until the person has been seen)
float32 person_speed      # m/s
float32 robot_speed       # m/s, commanded
